     .. versionadded:: 2.5
         Added new-style gettext support.
 
+Ordered Fallback Providers
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+``Environment.install_gettext_callables_with_fallback`` installs
+optional ordered chains with this signature::
+
+    install_gettext_callables_with_fallback(
+        gettext, ngettext, fallback_gettext_funcs=None,
+        fallback_ngettext_funcs=None, newstyle=None,
+        pgettext=None, npgettext=None, fallback_pgettext_funcs=None,
+        fallback_npgettext_funcs=None,
+    )
+
+Each fallback argument is a finite iterable of matching providers. The
+installer snapshots it, so later changes to a list do not change the
+installed chain. ``None`` or an empty iterable uses the normal
+installer.
+Non-empty contextual fallbacks require the corresponding ``pgettext``
+or ``npgettext`` primary and otherwise raise ``ValueError``.
+
+The primary runs first. A result equal to the source message indicates a
+miss; plural functions compare against the singular source for count 1
+and the plural source otherwise. Fallbacks run in order until one result
+differs. All misses return the selected source. Exceptions propagate and
+do not invoke later providers. Contextual providers receive the context
+on each attempt. Providers can use Jinja's context-aware decorators.
+
+Selection happens before existing new-style formatting and autoescaping.
+``newstyle=None`` preserves the current mode. Normal gettext chains work
+with direct calls and singular/plural ``trans`` blocks in either mode.
+Contextual chains support direct calls, not new ``trans`` syntax.
+Reinstallation replaces providers and chains; the normal uninstall
+method removes them. Applications not using this installer are
+unchanged.
+
+.. versionadded:: 3.1.0
+
 .. method:: jinja2.Environment.uninstall_gettext_translations()
 
     Uninstall the environment's globally installed translation.
